== Effects ==
* Sets the [[Devil Room#Conditions to make Devil Rooms appear|Devil Room chance]] to 100% regardless of all other modifiers, guaranteeing a {{R|Devil Room}} or {{R|Angel Room}} Door will spawn whenever possible and remain open.

== Notes ==
* Even if taken after a boss is killed, Goat Head will force a Devil / Angel Room door to spawn on that floor.
* Taking a deal with the Devil will prevent Angel Rooms from appearing, meaning Goat Head must be acquired from another source for an {{R|Angel Room}} to spawn.
* {{dlc|anr}} Goat Head will not force a Devil / Angel Room door to open if the boss fight was in a narrow room.
* {{dlc+|a}} Goat Head has no effect in [[Greed mode]] and is not normally available.
** It can still be a starting item for {{c|Eden}}, a bonus item from {{i|Eden's Blessing}}, and is obtainable with {{i|Pandora's Box}} and {{i|Sacrificial Altar}}.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} By touching the [[Fire Places#White Fire Place|white fire]] in {{s|Downpour}} II and {{s|Dross}} II, Isaac will temporarily become {{c|The Lost}}. After defeating the boss, Goat Head will always keep the devil deal door open, allowing the Lost to take one Devil Deal item for free.{{dlc-}}

== Synergies ==
* {{T|Black Feather}}: Grants a damage boost.
* {{i|Duality}}: Both Angel and Devil Room doors spawn after every boss, and the selected door will never disappear.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|Eucharist}}: Overrides Goat Head.

